+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_01QXCr9bqv9KkcBYyz1AoQ5U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's just an incidental lockfile normalization from `npm install`, unrelated to the bugs. Everything is clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nFound and fixed all 6 planted bugs:\n\n1. **`src/events/bus.ts`** — handler registry was a module-level `const` shared across *every* `EventBus` instance, so handlers from earlier tests/services leaked into later ones. Made it a per-instance property.\n2. **`src/orders/repository.ts`** — `update()` replaced the entire order with just the patch fields instead of merging, wiping out `items`, `customerId`, etc. on every update.\n3. **`src/orders/service.ts`** — `cancelOrder` emitted the cancellation event without a `status` field, but `InventoryService` requires `status === 'cancelled'` before releasing stock — so cancelled orders never released their reserved stock.\n4. **`src/orders/service.ts`** — refund window check used `>=` instead of `>`, rejecting refunds on exactly day 30 instead of only day 31+.\n5. **`src/billing/service.ts`** — `handleRefund` was registered without `.bind(this)`, causing `this.payments` to be undefined when the handler fired.\n6. **`src/billing/calculator.ts`** — intermediate discount/after-discount/tax values were rounded to cents before computing the next step, compounding rounding error; now the raw values flow through the calculation and rounding is applied only once, to each final output field.\n\nAll 34 tests pass, `npm run build` and `npm run lint` are clean."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":66937,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session